A||||20||carpetviper||Performance parts questions....||||5||
Z||000000||carpetviper||11-15-2001||03:38 PM||||Hey I'm still got a bit to learn about fiero and engines so any legitimate help would be appreciated. I'm looking to improve my '86 V6 SE's acceleration and overall performance without putting all of my money into it. Will any of these increase HP and acceleration and by how much? (These are all sold at the fierostore.com)<BR>V6 Performance Chip<BR>160* Thermostat<BR>176* fan switch<BR>V6 Cold Air Cone Intake<P>Thanks for your help!<p>[This message has been edited by carpetviper (edited 11-15-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||JohnF||11-15-2001||04:29 PM||||I'll take the flak on this one!  <P>All of these toys are "feel good" things for you to do to your Fiero.  Assuming you car is in good tuned-up and running condition, none of them will make much of a difference that you can notice.<P>Take that same money and time and remove your exhaust manifolds.  Port these smooth and let your engine breathe.  This will probably equate to more rear-wheel bang for the buck than all of the stuff above.||||reg||1
Z||000002||MinnGreenGT||11-15-2001||04:35 PM||||Powerwise... I'd suggest just getting a K&N air filter, removing the "waterbox" from behind the intake grill on the driver's side.  Then look into a "PowerPulley" from the Fiero Store.  Ummm... next would be a MSD 6al Electronic Ignition system.  Oh yeah, porting out the extra metal from inside the exhaust manifold makes a notable difference.  Then look into a Bored Out Throttlebody & Intake Manifold (Darrel Morse).  Those are quite a few of the lesser-expensive mods.<P>There is quite a bit of controversy over whether a "PowerChip" and "Cold-Air" intake make much difference... run a few searches in both Tech & General Discussion and decide for yourself- it's safer that way <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Oh yeah, welcome to the forum!<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||11-15-2001||04:57 PM||||Going to a lower temp thermostat without updating the ECM, will make your car run rich.  The stock ECM wants 195 for operation, or the car thinks its cold outside. Power chips are something you can say you have, but realistically add little noticable performance on a day to day running.<P>A good tune up, good wires, distributor cap, coil, timing set properly will be your best improvement. As a clean throttle body, port polished intake/ exhaust, headders, free flow exhaust, turbo, supercharger.. Oops, I got carried away..you don't want to spend all your money..||||reg||1
Z||000004||GSXPete||11-15-2001||05:06 PM||||besides those "sprint" headers that are nearly $600, are there any options other the porting the exhaust manifolds? <P>btw i do some porting myself. how much work is it to take the manifolds off? a matter of hours? Or is it like a whole weekend project where u have to move the motor around? thanks. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||JohnF||11-15-2001||05:15 PM||||Hey!  I haven't taken too much flak after all!  <P>Me too - Welcome to the forum.  However, we all will like it a lot when a newbie post a pix of the "new" Fiero.<P>Learn to use the "Search" function at the top of this page for most any subject you want to investigate - such as porting/power pulleys/throttle body mods, etc.  Try Ogre's Cave also at the top of this page and various web sites.  <P>It's amazing how much info there is!<P>||||reg||10
Z||000006||Kasdan||11-15-2001||06:45 PM||||The sprint manifolds on 1dst2m6's car lowered his Torque by ~15 while only raising his hp by ~4....not a good investment, just port-match your stock manifolds.<P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan, 1986 GT<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kassig2.gif">                  <BR>Aftermarket Power Steering, Rebuilt 2.8<BR>http://www.geocities.com/mtyler14/index.html||||reg||1
Z||000007||carpetviper||11-15-2001||09:15 PM||||Okay, how about this combo? A new distributor cap (old one has soem rust from last owner), new fuel filter(heard a new one works a bit better), a V-6 Power Pulley, and possible new plugs and wires(don't know when they were last changed). Will this do anything significant or just smart to do? Also does anyone know if V-6 ACCEL SUPER COIL (#51063 fierostore) does any different from the stock. Thanks again for your help guys. <P>BTW I'll try and get a pic of my fiero to post with my messages.<p>[This message has been edited by carpetviper (edited 11-15-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000008||camon||11-15-2001||11:34 PM||||The accel coil that the fiero store lists for 59.00 can be bought at pepboys or Advance Auto for like 40.00 or did I pay 49.99. So if you deside on the accel I would get it at pepboys or Advance auto (you'll save 10.00 right off the bat plus you won't need to worry about waiting and paying shipping)!<P>Anyway...there are some fiero owners that have had trouble with this coil (I haven't though). I noticed slightly better throttle response easier starting and smoother idle (didn't notice a power increase). I also changed plugs and went with the ACDELCO Rapid Fires.....I haven't had any trouble running them (and they are better then what was in it...champions) but wish I would have got the Bosche Platium +4's (heard they are better then the rapid fires....don't know how true it is).<P>------------------<BR>Keith||||reg||1
Z||000009||shark93726||11-16-2001||01:32 AM||||About the best HP increase for the money and work involved is to switch the rocker arms to Smal block chevy ones which are about 10% higher lift.  that gives the same effect as a higher lift cam without any engine disassembly, and from what I have read on it, will give better torque and horsepower through the entire rpm range and will still meet smog.<P>Don't take my word for it though, ask the guys here and the Fieroracinglist group, and you should be able to get the specifics.<P>Have fun.<P>Gerald Storvik (8shark.com)||||reg||1
Z||000010||carpetviper||11-16-2001||06:57 AM||||Anyone else have opinions on my list and the last two responses? Any assistance is well accepted, as I'd like to get the most bang for my buck.||||reg||3
Z||000011||olliver||11-16-2001||09:00 AM||||To bring the 2.8L alive in my '86GT this is what i've done.<P>Crane Cam 2030<BR>Crane Lifters<BR>Bored .060"<BR>Ceramic Coated Combustion Chambers<BR>Teflon Coated the Piston Skirts<BR>Knife Edged the Crank<BR>Chamfered the Oil Holes<BR>Higher Flow Oil Pump<BR>All New Sensors (Most Important)<BR>Painted Engine Yellow (I swear It makes It go Faster)<BR>Polyurathane Bushings (cradle, c/arms, sway bar)<P>2700 Stall Speed Torque Converter<BR>Tranny Cooler<P><BR>That was a hefty price tag, but hey it's worth it if you like the car you drive.<BR>And it was a far cry from going out and buying a brand new car.||||reg||1
Z||000012||avengador1||11-16-2001||09:02 AM||||Don't use the 160 degree thermostat, it will make your car run too rich, especially when it gets cold out side. I just replaced it in mine (160) to Rodney Dickmans 180 degree one. This will still give you some performance gains without sacrificing economy too much or reliability.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||carpetviper||11-16-2001||03:34 PM||||Just a random question, does anyone know about how much HP a 3800turbo would produce in a fiero?||||reg||1
Z||000014||carpetviper||11-17-2001||09:27 AM||||anyone?||||reg||5
Z||000015||avengador1||11-17-2001||11:28 AM||||The amount of horsepower gained by a turbo depends on how much boost pressure you are running. I believe a safe estimate would be anywhere from 20%(low boost)to 60%(med-high boost). I believe with these you would still have a streetable car. If you built the engine to be bullet proof it could be greater than 100% gain with very high boost.||||reg||1
Z||000016||carpetviper||11-22-2001||10:03 PM||||Here's my fiero. In the process of making yet another new sig. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carpetviper.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000017||WKDFIRO||11-23-2001||04:17 PM||||I would agree with JohnF 100% about the manifolds being the best performance for the time and money. Everything else, the ignition, the plugs etc are not as poorly designed as Fiero manifolds (and I speak of the 4 cylinder as well!) Just pull off the one exhaust manifold that you can get to and you will know exactly what we are talking about. <P>I would have liked to go to headers just to get away from the cracked manifolds but I have already lost a lot of back preasure from my custom exhaust job to lose any more. Too much flow is not such a great thing!<P>The rocker arms are another good improvement but you are still taking off the upper/intermediate intake manifolds, vacuum lines and injectors, which to some is a big job and to others a big pain just to get the valve covers off. (I still have yet to be convinced that the valve covers can be taken off with all that on!)<P>Hope this helps and welcome to the Forum. <BR>I would definitely suggest to do a search on "Aftermarket" as far as specific aftermarket performance.||||reg||1
Z||000018||artherd||11-24-2001||03:10 AM||||The valve covers can be taken off with just LOSENING the middle intake (you have to remove the phlenum of course...)<P>It's a half-day job to just pop the whole shebang off, fuel rail and injectors and all, though.  Not too bad.<P>PS: it's 30seconds on a Northstar, wow that 1-piece, bolts-directly-to-the-heads intake/velocity-stack/fuel-rail&injector/cool-aluminum-thing, is really neat!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by WKDFIRO:<BR><B>I would agree with JohnF 100% about the manifolds being the best performance for the time and money. Everything else, the ignition, the plugs etc are not as poorly designed as Fiero manifolds (and I speak of the 4 cylinder as well!) Just pull off the one exhaust manifold that you can get to and you will know exactly what we are talking about. <P>I would have liked to go to headers just to get away from the cracked manifolds but I have already lost a lot of back preasure from my custom exhaust job to lose any more. Too much flow is not such a great thing!<P>The rocker arms are another good improvement but you are still taking off the upper/intermediate intake manifolds, vacuum lines and injectors, which to some is a big job and to others a big pain just to get the valve covers off. (I still have yet to be convinced that the valve covers can be taken off with all that on!)<P>Hope this helps and welcome to the Forum. <BR>I would definitely suggest to do a search on "Aftermarket" as far as specific aftermarket performance.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000019||jubjub2m6||11-25-2001||12:30 AM||||that k&n cone filter thing that hangs off where the old stock box would be that thing is just garbage its to much for what you get.... goto <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cwestco.com</A>  its chris west's website with alot of fiero stuff on it they have a cold induction air intake system for like 175. its pretty cool setup it actually goes all the way down to the side intake and its more of a ram air effect to it..its really nice img onna get one once i get the money for it||||reg||1
Z||000020||lou_dias||11-25-2001||02:48 PM||||Lose toqrue with the sprint manifolds?<BR>I dynoed at 203 ft*lbs with those and a hollow cat and no muffler on my 3.4 conversion and a crane 2030 compucam.<BR>I'd hate to see how much torque I'd have it the exhaust was stock...||||reg||1
